<!-- =======================================================
     01 / CONTEXT
     ======================================================= -->

<CaseSection
  number="01"
  label="Context"
  title="Modernizing a faculty website that had become difficult to navigate and maintain."
  intro="FMIPA UGM initiated a full website redesign to replace an aging digital experience with a clearer, more responsive, and more maintainable system."
>
  <p>
    Over time, the existing website had accumulated
    several issues. Its interface felt visually
    outdated, some components and assets no longer
    behaved consistently, responsive behavior was
    limited, and parts of the website depended on
    paid assets that introduced recurring maintenance
    costs.
  </p>

  <p>
    The content structure had also become fragmented.
    Important information was spread across many
    pages, while several destinations were redundant
    or difficult to discover.
  </p>

  <p>
    The redesign therefore became more than a visual
    refresh. It was also an opportunity to reconsider
    how information should be organized and how
    visitors should move through the faculty website.
  </p>
</CaseSection>


