<!-- =======================================================
     05 / IMPLEMENTATION + VALIDATION
     ======================================================= -->

<CaseSection
  number="05"
  label="Implementation"
  title="Bringing the design into WordPress without relying on premium tooling."
>
  <p>
    Implementation introduced another layer of
    constraint. The website needed to rely on free
    WordPress plugins rather than premium
    dependencies, including Elementor Basic instead
    of Elementor Pro.
  </p>

  <p>
    Components that would normally be available
    through premium page-building tools therefore had
    to be implemented manually or hardcoded by the
    development team.
  </p>

  <h3>
    Frontend contribution
  </h3>

  <p>
    I contributed to frontend implementation and
    personally implemented the Organization Structure
    experience in WordPress, including lecturer
    profiles containing educational and research
    information.
  </p>

  <h3>
    User Acceptance Testing
  </h3>

  <p>
    The website went through three rounds of User
    Acceptance Testing with lecturers and faculty
    leadership.
  </p>

  <p>
    The core design direction remained largely intact.
    Feedback primarily resulted in smaller functional
    adjustments, editorial corrections, and content
    revisions.
  </p>
</CaseSection>


